Ellen (docs): Quick one 9: customers upgrading to sdk v2 keep asking for a concise migration note for context-fallbacks. We should show a minimal pattern: detect 429, honor Retry-After if present, drop oldest non-system messages until under target, retry with bounded backoff. Can someone sketch a tiny snippet + 1-line migration tip?

Omar (sdk): I9ll do a JS + py 1-paragraph + 2-line snippet. Recommendation: message-level trimming (not token gymnastics) and never remove system/instruction messages.

Jun (eng-runtime): +1. Runtime now sets `x-partial-ok: 1` when we return partial content; callers should log that header and reconcile before reapplying side-effects. Also `Retry-After` can be fractional; treat <1s as noise and use backoff instead.

Maya (devex): We9ll need two UX lines for the docs banner: 'Trying trimmed context...' and 'Retrying after backoff'. I can add translations for ES/FR after the copy lands.

Omar (sdk): Snippet draft (JS, super compact):

```js
// trim oldest non-system messages and retry on 429
async function sendWithTrim(client, convo, opts = {}) {
  let tries = 0;
  while (tries < (opts.maxRetries||3)) {
    try { return await client.generate({conversation: convo}); }
    catch (err) {
      if (err.status !== 429) throw err;
      const ra = parseFloat(err.headers?.['retry-after']||'0');
      await sleep(ra>=1?ra*1000:Math.pow(2,tries)*300 + Math.random()*100);
      // drop oldest non-system messages until under target
      while (convo.length && tokenCount(convo) > (opts.targetTokens||2500)) {
        if (convo[0].role === 'system') break; else convo.shift();
      }
      tries++;
    }
  }
  throw new Error('retries exhausted');
}
```

Omar (sdk): Py variant pushed in PR description. Kept it short per docs guidance.

Jun (eng-runtime): Please add a one-line operator note: "If your app applies side-effects on model output, validate partial responses (check `x-partial-ok` / `err.partialResponse`) before retrying to avoid duplicates."

Ellen (docs): Good. I9ll add a bold callout: "Do not trim system/instruction messages." and a tiny migration tip: "Swap ad-hoc handlers for sdk.retryUtils.trimAndRetry to get same behavior across languages."

Maya (devex): I'll attach the translations after merge. Also can we link to sdk retry util: /sdk/src/retry-utils.ts in the PR?

